From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pyproject: relax three more tree-sitter grammar pins for
 riscv64

Same problem as the tree-sitter pin itself (patch 0002): pyproject.toml
pins tree-sitter-rust==0.24.0, tree-sitter-c-sharp==0.23.1, and
tree-sitter-language-pack==1.13.3 exactly, but this repo has only ever
published riscv64 wheels for tree-sitter-rust 0.24.2, tree-sitter-c-sharp
0.23.5, and tree-sitter-language-pack 1.15.8+ (docs/packages/*.yaml).
With PIP_ONLY_BINARY=:all:, installing the built wheel fails:

    ERROR: Could not find a version that satisfies the requirement
    tree-sitter-rust==0.24.0 (from openviking) (from versions: 0.24.2)
    ERROR: No matching distribution found for tree-sitter-rust==0.24.0

Relax all three to a lower bound for the same reason patch 0002 relaxes
tree-sitter itself: this port's own test coverage never touches these
grammar packages' Python APIs directly, so the exact-pin "avoid
unvalidated upstream API and grammar changes" concern doesn't apply here.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64-wheel availability is specific to this port; upstream's own CI never resolves against a riscv64 index]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -67,9 +67,9 @@ dependencies = [
     "tree-sitter-typescript==0.23.2",
     "tree-sitter-java==0.23.5",
     "tree-sitter-cpp==0.23.4",
-    "tree-sitter-rust==0.24.0",
+    "tree-sitter-rust>=0.24.0",
     "tree-sitter-go==0.25.0",
-    "tree-sitter-c-sharp==0.23.1",
+    "tree-sitter-c-sharp>=0.23.1",
     "tree-sitter-php==0.24.1",
     "tree-sitter-lua==0.5.0",
     # OpenTelemetry
@@ -85,7 +85,7 @@ dependencies = [
     "mcp>=1.27,<2",
     "pathspec>=1.1.1",
     "grep-ast==0.9.0",
-    "tree-sitter-language-pack==1.13.3",
+    "tree-sitter-language-pack>=1.13.3",
 ]
 
 
